  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe current solution uses simulated annealing, which can be slow and prone to local optima. We propose using a multi-start optimization method that combines local search around the initial parent and global exploration via radial basis function (RBF) interpolation. This approach balances exploration and exploitation by leveraging RBF for interpolation and Bayesian optimization with expected improvement. The key improvement is using a more sophisticated local optimization strategy applied to a subset of candidates generated by adaptive repair functions, ensuring good scalability and avoidance of local optima.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n- Representation: Step function with `n_points/2` samples over [0,2]\n- Variables: h[i] \u2208 [0,1] for all i\n- Objective: Minimize C_5 = max_k (integral of h(x)(1-h(x+k)) dx)\n- Constraints: Integral of h(x) dx = 1\n- Objective computation: Use correlation of extended function (h_full = [h, h_reversed]) with (1-h_full), then maximum element multiplied by dx\n- Repair functions: Scaling and clipping to enforce constraints\n- Search space: n_points/2 dimensional space, using RBF for interpolation and expected improvement for acquisition\n\n3. Implementation procedure\n   a. Initialization\n      - If initial_h_values is available, use parent; else tent function via:\n        def initial_h(n_points):\n            x = np.linspace(0,2,n_points)\n            return np.clip(1 - np.abs(x-1), 0, 1)[:n_points//2]\n      - Integral_target = n_points/4\n      - Repair function: Scaling and clipping ensuring integral constraint via mapping [sum(h)] to [integral target]\n\n   b. RBF Interpolation Setup\n      - Transform samples to [0,1]^m (m = n_points/2) via:\n        def map_to_hypercube(x):\n            m = (x - x.min())/(x.max() - x.min())\n            return m\n      - Use RBF kernel: \u03c6(x) = exp(-\u03b3||x(u)-x(v)||\u00b2)\n      - Optimization: Expected improvement acquisition function\n      - RBF parameters: e\u00b3 (\u03b5=1e-4)\n\n   c. Core Optimization Loop\n      - Temperature schedule: Linear cooling from 1 to 1e-2 over 10,000 iterations\n      - Main loop with patience 1000 for plateau detection\n      - Three phases per iteration:\n        1. Local minimization (Nelder-Mead) on random samples from RBF model, restart if plateau\n        2. Repair validity and maximize EI on RBF predictions\n        3. Simulated annealing with cooling schedule\n\n   d. Termination\n      - Budget monitoring: 100s budget\n      - Convergence criteria: No improvement for 2 periods (1000 iterations)\n      - Best candidate saved during optimization\n\n   e. Candidate Generation\n      - Random walk with drift towards previous best via:\n        def proposal(x_best=None, x=None):\n            if x_best is None: return x + np.random.normal(0, 0.1, len(x))\n            return x + 0.1*(x_best - x) + np.random.normal(0, 0.01, len(x))\n      - Repair candidates: Ensure valid candidates via clipping/scale\n\n   f. Evaluation\n      - Repair function: \n        def repair(h):\n            s = np.sum(h)\n            if s <= 0: return np.clip(h*1e1, 0, 1)  # Emergency repair\n            return np.clip(h*(integral_target/s), 0, 1)\n      - Safe repair: Notify on constraint violation but continue optimization\n\n   g. Learning/Schedule\n      - Log acceptance rate between 0.4 and 0.6\n      - Cubic exploration: Probability decreases with iterations\n      - Data collection: Store all samples for thorough exploration\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\n   a. Initialization\n      - Initial optimization period: i_min=2000\n      - Candidates: 20 random samples + surrounding region\n      - Gaussian RBF parameters: \u03b3=10 (length scales)\n\n   b. Repair strategy\n      - Conductive repair: Bias towards parent use\n      - Preventive repair: Scale before if out-of-bounds\n\n   c. Optimization variance\n      - Simulated annealing cooling: 0.9995 per 1000 iterations\n      - Random jump factor: 0.25, 0.5, 0.75\n\n   d. Exploration variance\n      - a=2, b=0.5 for acceptance rate learning\n      - Patience window: 500 iterations\n\n   e. Interpolation periods\n      - Default 2 periods per 10,000 iterations\n      - Maximum evaluations: 50000 (budget)\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n   - Dominant cost: 280^2 operations per objective\n   - Budget estimation: 1e4 evaluations in 100s using Pyton\n   - Early termination: When no improvement for 2 periods\n   - Robust constraints: Repair always\n   - Sleep phase: 1 (no network)\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n   - Pre-optimization: Validate initial construction\n   - Objectives: Minimize C5\n   - Validation: Scipy.optimize.minimize for fallback\n   - Final reset: Re-verify candidate\n   - Execution checks: Skip if memory exhausted\n   - Unique seed: 42 (adjustable)\n   - Sample size: 280 points\n   - Repair confirmation: Ensure valid candidates\n   - Convergence report: Probability and accepted candidates",
